5652	SEC-SQL-PAT-001-RC14	oracle	Clarify Oracle licensing and support for version upgrades	SEC-SQL-PAT-001-RC14-oracle	Oracle-specific resolution: Organizations uncertain about licensing implications, support pricing for extended support, or cloud service EOL timelines delay decision-making. **Organizational Root Causes:** - **Absence of strategic technology refresh planning** – Organizations lack formal EOL roadmaps or capital planning processes that account for database lifecycle management as a regular operational cost. - **Siloed responsibilities across infrastructure, application development, and security teams** – No single team owns database lifecycle management, so responsibility falls through cracks with no accountability for proactive upgrades. - **Reactive security culture** – Organizations respond to security incidents rather than proactively addressing known risks, treating EOL databases as acceptable until a breach occurs. - **Inadequate governance and compliance frameworks** – Lack of formal change control processes or compliance audits that would flag EOL systems as non-compliant and trigger action. - **Technical debt accumulation** – Years of deferred maintenance across infrastructure, applications, and processes create organizational inertia that makes large system changes feel impossible. - **Poor communication between business and technology** – Business leaders don't understand the security and operational risks of EOL systems, so budget requests for upgrades are frequently rejected. - **Understaffing in database administration and DevOps** – Organizations operate with minimal DBA or infrastructure staff, leaving no capacity for proactive work beyond firefighting production issues.	supervised	medium	Resolves: Vendor licensing and support service uncertainty	authored	\N	t	\N	\N	2026-02-28 22:39:08.596677	2026-02-28 22:39:08.596677
5653	SEC-SQL-PAT-002-RC01	oracle	Implement Oracle database asset discovery and patch inventory	SEC-SQL-PAT-002-RC01-oracle	Oracle-specific resolution: Organizations lack comprehensive visibility into which database servers exist, their exact versions, and their current patch levels, making it impossible to patch systems they don't know exist.	supervised	medium	Resolves: Incomplete asset discovery and inventory	authored	\N	t	\N	\N	2026-02-28 22:39:08.596677	2026-02-28 22:39:08.596677
