13008	SEC-SQL-PRI-001-RC14	mariadb	Resolve: Detect active transactions touching sensitive columns (mysql)	resolve-pii-active-tx-mariadb	Live transactions are reading or modifying columns whose names indicate PII (password, ssn, credit card, email, etc.). Immediate actions: (1) audit which logins, hosts, and applications appear in results — confirm each is authorised to access PII; (2) enforce column-level access controls (MSSQL DENY/GRANT, Oracle VPD/Label Security, Postgres column GRANTs, MySQL column privileges); (3) apply dynamic data masking for non-privileged users (MSSQL Dynamic Data Masking, Oracle Data Redaction, pg_anonymizer, MySQL views); (4) ensure DAM logging captures all access to sensitive columns; (5) review whether application code truly needs unmasked PII or whether it can be tokenised/hashed.	supervised	critical	\N	authored	\N	t	\N	\N	2026-05-11 22:17:39.229791	2026-05-11 22:17:39.229791
